proof_bodies['n10-t4-cubic']=r'<p>For every pure spin-five vector, an exact identity expresses \(\lVert\psi\rVert^6\) as a rational linear combination of twenty cubic scalar contractions of its spin multipoles. Every term contains a multipole of rank \(1\le L\le4\). Fourth-order anticoherence would make the entire right-hand side zero, contradicting \(\lVert\psi\rVert^6=1\).</p><p>Two independent exact calculations establish the identity: one on the symmetric three-copy space, and one by expanding all polynomial coefficients in arbitrary complex amplitudes. No symmetry ansatz or numerical tolerance is used in the final certificate.</p><p><a href="./research/reported-exclusions/index.html#n10">Read the complete identity and proof ↗</a> · <a href="./research/reported-exclusions/n10-t4/certificate.json">Exact certificate</a> · <a href="./research/reported-exclusions/n10-t4/verify.py">Independent verifier</a></p>'
